## Original Content
At Netflix, October isn&#8217;t just for scary movies; it&#8217;s also for funny documentaries. The streamer will premiere four feature docs celebrating some of comedy&#8217;s most influential voices and institutions, with one film rolling out each week in October. Debuting on Oct. 7 is &#8220;Who Is Martin Mull?,&#8221; from the late Bob Saget and Neil Berkeley. [&#8230;]

## Summary
Netflix will premiere four comedy documentaries in October, releasing one per week. The first, 'Who Is Martin Mull?' directed by the late Bob Saget and Neil Berkeley, debuts on Oct. 7. Other comedy docs are also planned for the month.

## Key Points
- Netflix is premiering four feature documentaries celebrating influential comedy voices and institutions in October
- One comedy documentary will roll out each week throughout the month
- 'Who Is Martin Mull?' premieres on Oct. 7, directed by the late Bob Saget and Neil Berkeley


